{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-interpretation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-interpretation","kind":"remark","title":"Why the odd moments do not vanish","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis","tags":["hecke","blitvic","crossing-exponent","pair-partition"],"text":"hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-interpretation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-interpretation\"></a><p>The obstruction comes from the quadratic relation. A repeated generator does not reduce to the identity: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma^{2} = h\\sigma + 1</code> leaves a term in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma</code> itself, and a non-zero linear term survives in every power. A <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q,t)</code>-Gaussian has a symmetric moment sequence. The centred Hecke generator has eigenvalues <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q - z</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-q^{-1} - z</code>, which are not negatives of each other, so its distribution under <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}</code> is not symmetric.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-interpretation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"7.3.14","page":"b/rem-hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-interpretation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":62,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
